The Mournland is what remains of [[Cyre]], the nation destroyed on the Day of Mourning (Olarune 20, 994 YK). A wall of dead-grey mist marks its borders. Inside, the laws of nature function erratically.

!! The Mourning
The exact cause remains unknown. Leading theories:
* A weapon of mass destruction (possibly Cannith or Aundairian)
* Planar breach (Mabar or Xoriat)
* Divine judgment
* Collective magical backlash from the [[Last War]]

The [[Mournland Expedition]] of 998 YK confirmed the interior is habitable but deeply hostile. Wounds do not heal inside the Mournland. Bodies of the fallen do not decay. The landscape is warped and crystallized in mid-destruction.

!! Inhabitants
* [[The Lord of Blades]] leads a warforged nation in the interior
* Mutated survivors (the "ghosts of Cyre")
* Preserved Cyran military units, still fighting a war that ended

!! Strategic Importance
The Mournland contains vast pre-war Cyran military infrastructure, magical repositories, and — according to some sources — the [[Vault of Whispers]].

!! Connections
* [[Cyre]] (former nation)
* [[The Lord of Blades]] (current claimant)
* [[Lady Elaydren d'Cannith]] (interest in Cannith sites within)
* [[The Vault of Whispers]] (rumored location)
